flowchart TB
  %% diagram: overview
  VSC["VS Code<br/>software engineers"]
  IJ["IntelliJ IDEA<br/>Java engineers"]
  SM["SageMaker Studio<br/>data scientists, beside the data<br/><i>CLI in the terminal · Agent SDK in a cell</i>"]
  TERM["Any terminal<br/>site reliability engineers<br/><i>reads allowlisted — investigate freely</i><br/><i>any change waits for a human to approve it</i>"]

  subgraph GOVERNED["Policy lives in the repo — what a session may read,<br/>run and change, reviewed like any other change —<br/>plus managed settings from MDM and your IdP"]
    CC["<b>Claude Code</b><br/>the same tool, the same policy,<br/>wherever the work already happens"]
  end

  subgraph GCP["GCP"]
    GCPAPP["Customer-facing web"]
    GCPOBS["Logs · metrics · deploy state"]
  end
  subgraph TOOLING["Reached by skill or MCP server"]
    GH["GitHub — review and CI<br/><i>the gh CLI, and an MCP server</i><br/><b>GitHub Actions</b> — the tests run on every PR"]
    JIRA["Jira — the delivery record<br/><i>a skill, driving the REST API</i>"]
    SLACK["Slack — where readouts land<br/><i>MCP server</i>"]
    IDEMCP["The IDE itself — diagnostics, open file<br/><i>MCP server</i>"]
    FREDSK["Market data — FRED · <i>a skill, wrapping the REST API</i> · the credential is loaded, never printed<br/>fetch, align and cite — the analysis is the analyst's"]
    %% invisible links keep this group wide rather than tall, so it fits a slide:
    %% GH/JIRA, SLACK/IDEMCP and FREDSK end up as three columns two rows deep
    %% instead of one long stack.
    %% A full-width FREDSK spanning the columns underneath was tried and is not
    %% available: mermaid caps a node's width at flowchart.wrappingWidth (200px by
    %% default) and dagre has no column spanning, so a long line wraps instead of
    %% stretching. Raising wrappingWidth to 420 does widen it — and takes the whole
    %% diagram from 2466x1116 to 3152x942, an aspect of 3.35 against a slide's 1.78,
    %% which renders everything ~28% smaller. Height is not the binding constraint
    %% here; width is. Measured 2026-08-22 — do not re-litigate without re-measuring.
    GH ~~~ SLACK
    JIRA ~~~ IDEMCP
    SLACK ~~~ FREDSK
    IDEMCP ~~~ FREDSK
  end
  subgraph LEFTCOL[" "]
    subgraph PLANE["Model calls · device policy"]
    BR["<b>Claude on AWS Bedrock (or GCP)</b><br/>inference runs in your own AWS account<br/>AWS SSO, IAM, CloudTrail, VPC endpoints<br/>PAYG on existing AWS agreement<br/>zero data retention<br/><i>+ Claude apps gateway: model and managed<br/>settings per IdP group, spend limits</i>"]
    MDM["<b>MDM — Jamf or Intune</b><br/>fleet delivery of endpoint/gateway"]
    end
    subgraph AWS["AWS"]
      AWSAPP["Payments services"]
      AWSOBS["Application logs · metrics · deploy state"]
      CWCC["<b>CloudWatch — Claude Code usage</b><br/>native OTLP endpoints, no collector<br/>sessions · tokens · cost · active time<br/>commits · PRs · lines changed<br/>edit-permission decisions<br/><i>behavioural signal only — prompt content off</i>"]
    end
  end

  VSC --> CC
  IJ --> CC
  SM --> CC
  TERM --> CC

  %% MDM sits at Claude Code's own rank so the group top-aligns with the policy
  %% box. Any VISIBLE edge from CC would force MDM a rank lower (dagre ranks by
  %% edge direction, and this mermaid has no reversed arrow), so the rank is set
  %% by an invisible link from a top-row node instead. Measured 2026-08-23 — see D31.
  VSC ~~~ MDM
  MDM ~~~ BR
  CC ==>|"every model call"| BR
  CC <-->|"the tools around the code"| TOOLING
  CC ==>|"build and deploy"| AWSAPP
  CC ==>|"build and deploy"| GCPAPP
  CC -->|"OTLP direct — how the tool itself is measured"| CWCC
  AWSOBS -.->|"read-only — what an SRE investigates with"| CC
  GCPOBS -.->|"read-only"| CC

  style LEFTCOL fill:none,stroke:none
  style TOOLING fill:#f6f4ff,stroke-dasharray:4
  style PLANE fill:#f6f4ff,stroke-dasharray:4
  style GOVERNED fill:#f6f4ff,stroke-width:2px
  classDef hub stroke-width:3px;
  classDef plane stroke-width:2px;
  class CC hub;
  class BR plane;
